      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Necessary evil\" is a pretty strong way to put it. It sounds like you're saying transparency is basically secondary to executive power. \n\nIf I'm in a moot court and I bring up the massive risk of corruption or the fact that past administrations have used this to hide illegal activities, how would you defend that position? Is there actually a legitimate legal argument for the other side that isn't just \"oversight is bad,\" or is the expansion of privilege just objectively the more functional path for a modern state?",
